WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:17.224
The Tang Monk jumped to his feet as the villagers hid behind trees.

2
00:00:18.704 --> 00:00:21.585
Wukong, Wujing, and Bajie pulled out their weapons.

3
00:00:22.866 --> 00:00:25.006
A large shell rose from the water.

4
00:00:25.026 --> 00:00:27.667
"It's a giant turtle!"

5
00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:28.667
said Bajie.

6
00:00:29.727 --> 00:00:31.788
The turtle bowed its head toward Wukong.

7
00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:35.769
"That demon had taken over my house and river.

8
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.210
Thank you for getting rid of him."

9
00:00:39.131 --> 00:00:40.951
The turtle then looked at the villagers.

10
00:00:42.332 --> 00:00:43.993
don't need to make a boat.

11
00:00:45.293 --> 00:00:47.554
I can take the travelers across the river."

12
00:00:49.075 --> 00:00:50.655
wonderful!" said the Tang Monk.

13
00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:56.698
"I'm from the Tang Empire, "I know who you are," interrupted the turtle.

14
00:00:56.718 --> 00:01:01.540
"You're traveling to the Western Paradise to get scriptures from Buddha.

15
00:01:03.057 --> 00:01:05.118
knew you would cross my river eventually.

16
00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.239
Climb onto my shell."

17
00:01:09.381 --> 00:01:11.122
eyed the turtle suspiciously.

18
00:01:11.142 --> 00:01:13.804
"How do we know we can trust you?

19
00:01:14.745 --> 00:01:18.427
Demons all along the way are waiting for my master to pass by."

20
00:01:18.447 --> 00:01:22.270
"They all want to eat him," added Bajie.

21
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.953
"I promise I won't hurt the Tang Monk," said the turtle.

22
00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:30.996
"I want to help him reach the Western Paradise."

23
00:01:35.388 --> 00:01:39.971
After a little more hesitation, the travelers stepped onto the turtle's shell.

24
00:01:41.492 --> 00:01:43.073
The turtle began to paddle.

25
00:01:44.494 --> 00:01:47.417
The villagers came out from behind the trees and waved.

26
00:01:48.537 --> 00:01:50.198
"Good-bye!" called a woman.

27
00:01:50.218 --> 00:01:53.221
"Please visit us on your way home!"

28
00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:54.601
shouted someone else.

29
00:01:54.622 --> 00:01:56.943
"We will, I promise!"

30
00:01:57.223 --> 00:01:57.964
called the monk.

31
00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.166
the turtle was far from shore.

32
00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.848
Bajie fell asleep.

33
00:02:04.908 --> 00:02:06.989
The turtle glanced back at the Tang Monk.

34
00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.471
"Excuse me, but can you do me a favor?"

35
00:02:12.052 --> 00:02:13.353
course," said the monk.

36
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:15.314
"What do you need me to do?"

37
00:02:16.454 --> 00:02:20.517
"I have been a good Buddhist for over a thousand years," said the turtle.

38
00:02:20.537 --> 00:02:23.939
"But sadly I'm still just a turtle.

39
00:02:24.779 --> 00:02:27.801
Can you ask Buddha when I will be reborn as a human?"

40
00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:29.862
Tang Monk nodded.

41
00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.563
"I will ask him."

42
00:02:32.643 --> 00:02:35.825
A few hours later, the turtle reached the other side of the river.

43
00:02:37.186 --> 00:02:39.547
The travelers stepped onto dry land.

44
00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:43.308
"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

45
00:02:44.509 --> 00:02:46.430
"You're welcome," said the turtle.

46
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.431
"Please don't forget to ask Buddha about me."

47
00:02:50.432 --> 00:02:52.553
The turtle disappeared under the water.

48
00:02:55.494 --> 00:02:59.616
The Tang Monk climbed onto the horse, and the group continued on the road.

49
00:03:01.724 --> 00:03:04.385
usual, Bajie soon started complaining.

50
00:03:04.405 --> 00:03:07.307
"I'm tired of walking already.

51
00:03:08.347 --> 00:03:10.968
I wish we could ride that turtle the whole way to the West."

52
00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:14.770
complaining," said Wukong.

53
00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.611
"Be happy that the road is flat here."

54
00:03:19.712 --> 00:03:21.653
They walked for another couple of hours.

55
00:03:22.633 --> 00:03:26.274
The road started to go up a mountain, getting steeper and steeper.

56
00:03:27.895 --> 00:03:31.889
The pig moaned, "The road isn't flat anymore!"

57
00:03:32.949 --> 00:03:35.050
A cold wind whipped past them.

58
00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:38.331
"Brr!" Wujing shivered.

59
00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.112
"Look!" said the Tang Monk, pointing.

60
00:03:42.613 --> 00:03:45.214
up the mountain was a large monastery.

61
00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:47.195
"Maybe we can rest there."

62
00:03:48.956 --> 00:03:50.076
looked at the monastery.

63
00:03:51.236 --> 00:03:53.077
A dark mist hung over it.

64
00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:56.539
The monkey shook his head.

65
00:03:57.659 --> 00:03:58.539
a bad place.

66
00:03:58.839 --> 00:04:00.848
We're not going there."

67
00:04:00.928 --> 00:04:02.869
"It looks fine to me," said the monk.

68
00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.651
"I can see things that humans can't see," said Wukong.

69
00:04:06.671 --> 00:04:10.073
"And I see a dark mist hanging over that monastery.

70
00:04:10.953 --> 00:04:12.294
A demon could be in there."

71
00:04:13.655 --> 00:04:15.636
There was a sudden growling sound.

72
00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:18.798
Wukong looked around to see what had caused it.

73
00:04:20.258 --> 00:04:21.159
patted his stomach.

74
00:04:21.179 --> 00:04:23.540
"Sorry, I'm a bit hungry."

75
00:04:25.621 --> 00:04:28.243
"We're all tired and hungry," said the Tang Monk.

76
00:04:29.063 --> 00:04:30.544
"We should just go to that monastery."

77
00:04:32.158 --> 00:04:33.341
said Wukong sharply.

78
00:04:33.361 --> 00:04:34.623
"Stay here.

79
00:04:34.884 --> 00:04:36.006
I will find food for us."

80
00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:42.379
He looked at the monk and warned him again, "Do not go to that monastery!"
